ARLIKAT PLATFORM - COMPLETE FEATURE LIST
Compiled 2026-08-21 from the arlikatweb codebase (branch phase_2)


WHAT THIS PRODUCT ACTUALLY IS
=============================

The UI calls itself "Arlikat-CRM", but that name undersells it. What is
built is a single-database business platform covering four operational
areas that are normally four separate purchases:

  1. CRM / Sales      - lead to cash
  2. Purchase         - indent to supplier payment
  3. Inventory        - warehouse, serial/batch, spares
  4. Service / FSM    - installed base, AMC, complaints, field engineers

The thing that makes it unusual is that these are not four products
glued together. A serial number received on a GRN becomes an asset at
a customer site, that asset sits under a warranty, the warranty rolls
into an AMC, the AMC generates preventive-maintenance schedules and
billing schedules, a customer complaint against that asset becomes a
work order, the engineer raises a spare indent on the work order, the
indent pulls stock out of the same warehouse, and the consumption
lands on the service bill. One chain, one system, no re-keying.

Scale of what exists today (counted, not estimated):
  - 298 entity modules in the Angular frontend
  - 4 role-specific dashboards (Sales, Service, Inventory, Purchase)
  - ~50 dedicated report screens with Excel + PDF export
  - Angular 14 SPA on Spring Boot (JHipster 7.9.3), multi-tenant MySQL


------------------------------------------------------------
1. CRM AND SALES
------------------------------------------------------------

Accounts (customers)
  - Account master with category, type, ownership, turnover band,
    industry type, region
  - Multiple billing addresses, shipping addresses and additional
    addresses per account
  - Contacts info tab on the account (every contact of that customer
    visible from the account screen)
  - Accounts list report, Customer 360 report

Contacts
  - Contact master with contact types
  - Per-contact billing and shipping addresses
  - Contact inventory / contact-to-account mapping
  - Contacts list report

Leads
  - Lead master with type, subtype, source, stage, status
  - Lost reason capture
  - Assignment to users (lead-asgn-to)
  - Competitor tagging per lead (which competitor you were up against)
  - Multiple contacts per lead, plus account-contact mapping
  - Lead conversion into account + contact + opportunity, with the
    conversion trail stored
  - Leads list report

Opportunities
  - Opportunity master with stages and probability-style pipeline
  - Product lines on the opportunity
  - Competitor tagging per opportunity
  - Billing and shipping addresses
  - Assignment to users
  - Opportunity to Quote conversion, Opportunity to Sales Order
    conversion, both with mapped product lines
  - Opportunity summary report, opportunity detailed report,
    opportunity conversion report

Quotations
  - Quote master with quote stages and numbering series
  - Product lines, additional charges, terms and conditions blocks
  - Buyback lines (customer trades in an old machine against the new
    one) - rare in generic CRMs, essential in equipment sales
  - Three separate approval streams: margin approval, document
    approval, request approval
  - Quote to Sales Order conversion with charge and product carry-over
  - Quotation summary + quotation detailed reports

Sales Orders
  - SO master with stages and numbering series
  - Products, additional charges, terms, buyback, attached documents
  - Margin / document / request approvals
  - SO to Invoice conversion
  - SO to Purchase Order conversion (including buyback products) - the
    "sell first, then procure" flow dealers actually run
  - Sales order summary, sales order detailed, sales review report,
    open order risk analysis

Proforma Invoice
  - PI master with PI types and numbering series
  - Products, additional charges, terms, billing and shipping addresses
  - Assignment

Invoices
  - Invoice master with invoice types and numbering series
  - Products, additional charges, terms
  - Bill-to, ship-to and dispatch-from addresses held separately
  - Margin, document and request approvals
  - E-invoice generation with IRN and QR code, and the raw e-invoice
    response payload stored for audit (einvoice-resp-data)
  - E-way bill fields
  - Invoice cancellation with a cancellation report
  - Invoice summary, invoice detailed, e-invoice report

Credit / Debit notes
  - Sales credit note and debit note, plus separate spare credit and
    spare debit for the service side
  - Credit note report

Money in
  - Payments with payment modes and quantity-pay types
  - Receivables report, advances report, applied invoice/bill report
  - Customer business analysis report

Sales activities
  - Activity master with type, subtype, status
  - Assignment, activity inventory link
  - Activity list report

Sales targets and performance
  - Per-user sales targets, target tenures, target frequencies
  - Actual vs Target visualisation on the CRM dashboard
  - Sales financial year separate from the accounting financial year

Approval engine (used across quote / SO / invoice / PO / bill / DC)
  - Sales approval setup + per-user approval setup
  - Margin-gated approvals (discount beyond X needs approval)
  - Document approvals and request approvals as separate tracks
  - Approval log visible on the record, approval status widget on the
    dashboard

Terms and conditions library
  - Reusable T&C blocks, assignable by group and by user, pulled into
    quotes, SOs, invoices, POs


