4. SERVICE AND FIELD SERVICE MANAGEMENT
------------------------------------------------------------

This is the part no horizontal CRM or ERP in this price band does
properly, and it is the reason the product exists.

Installed base / Assets
  - Asset master tied to customer, site and serial number
  - Asset category, subcategory, type, criticality, rating
  - Bulk upload of assets
  - Asset 360 report (everything that ever happened to one machine)
  - Asset summary report

Warranty
  - Warranty records with warranty types, covered products, documents,
    billing and site addresses, assignment
  - Warranty management report
  - Warranty expiry feeds the AMC prospect pipeline

AMC (annual maintenance contracts)
  - AMC master with contract type, AMC type, AMC stages
  - Asset-level AMC with asset ratings and asset replacement tracking
  - Auto-renewal rules, minimum cost rules, annual price-hike rules
  - Billing schedule (what to invoice, when, for how much)
  - PMS schedule (which preventive visits are due, when)
  - AMC to Billing, AMC to PMS, AMC to Service PI conversions
  - Approval log, comments, documents
  - AMC management report

Complaint management (CMS)
  - Complaint master with category, priority, status, event type
  - SLA info attached to the complaint
  - Spare info and live spare stock visible on the complaint
  - Replacement history for the machine
  - Product stock and spare stock lookups inline
  - CMS to Work Order, CMS to DC, CMS to Purchase Order conversions
  - CMS management report, SLA compliance report

Work Orders (the engineer's screen)
  - WO master with work order types and stages
  - EFSR - Engineer Field Service Report captured on the work order
  - Spare indent requests, split into service indents and repair
    indents
  - Indent to DC conversion and GRN conversion (spare goes out,
    replaced part comes back)
  - Serial and batch selection on consumption
  - Track Status timeline, comments, documents, change log
  - Reference details and estimation info tabs
  - Work order management report, engineer performance report,
    engineer spare consumption report, replacement machine report

Preventive maintenance
  - PM master with preventive stages and statuses
  - Schedules generated from AMC
  - PM management report

Installation management (IMS)
  - Installation records with installation type, stage, status
  - Work Order info tab on the installation
  - IMS management report

Service estimation and billing
  - Estimation with estimate types and estimation stages
  - Estimation vs Invoice report (did we bill what we quoted)
  - Service billing with billing types, detailed and management
    reports
  - Service PI

SLA and escalation
  - SLA definitions
  - Escalation matrix
  - Business hours and holiday setup so SLA clocks respect working
    time
  - SLA status on the service dashboard with achievement percentage

Service dashboard
  - Revenue pipeline: estimation and AMC value, billed value,
    outstanding value, with totals
  - Outstanding aging split by estimation and AMC (0-30, 31-60,
    61-90, 90+)
  - AMC prospects and forecast: warranties due now / 30 / 60 / 90 days,
    AMCs due now / 30 / 60 / 90, bills due now / 30 / 60 / 90 - each in
    quantity and value. This is the renewal-leakage killer.
  - Complaint status: total, unscheduled, scheduled, in progress,
    hold, completed
  - PM status: total, unscheduled, scheduled, in progress, completed,
    overdue
  - Installation status: total, unscheduled, scheduled, in progress,
    under review, closed
  - SLA status: active, achieved, at risk, breached, hold, with
