8. HONEST GAPS - READ THIS BEFORE WRITING ANY MARKETING COPY
------------------------------------------------------------

Do not claim these. They are the roadmap, not the product.

  - No general ledger / trial balance / balance sheet. There are
    payments, payables, receivables and expenses, but this is not an
    accounting package. It sits alongside Tally, it does not replace
    it. There is also no proven Tally or Zoho Books connector yet.
  - No native mobile app. Engineers use a responsive web app. That is
    genuinely workable but it is not an app-store app, and there is no
    offline mode - which matters for basement plant rooms and rural
    sites.
  - No engineer scheduling map, no route optimisation, no live
    technician GPS tracking. Assignment is manual.
  - No customer self-service portal. Customers cannot log a complaint
    or see their AMC status themselves.
  - No WhatsApp notifications (zero references in the code). Email
    and in-app only. For Indian field service this is the single
    highest-value gap to close.
  - No public API documentation, no webhook layer, no integration
    marketplace.
  - No payment gateway collection link on invoices.
  - Single language (English only, i18n scaffolding exists).

Sequence in which closing these unlocks the most sales:
  1. WhatsApp notifications (complaint acknowledgement, engineer
     assigned, AMC expiry, payment reminder)
  2. Customer self-service portal (raise complaint, see AMC, see
     invoices)
  3. Tally / accounting export
  4. Native engineer app with offline capture
  5. Public API + webhooks
